{"term":"forge","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:62b734b8ef4c5ef250","definition":"A furnace or hearth where metals are heated prior to hammering them into shape.","example":"Close to the hump-backed bridge on the lane leading into the Hambleden Valley is a mid-19th-century smithy, its inside walls hung with tools of the blacksmith's trade, though decorative wrought-ironwork is now the main product from its glowing forge.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["American forge","brute de forge","Catalan forge","Clifton Forge","Consall Forge","forge-hammer","forgelike","forgeman","forgemaster","Forge Valley","forge wagon","microforge","Old Forge","software forge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6cccebd4e31279c529","definition":"A workshop in which metals are shaped by heating and hammering them.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["smithy","smithery"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["American forge","brute de forge","Catalan forge","Clifton Forge","Consall Forge","forge-hammer","forgelike","forgeman","forgemaster","Forge Valley","forge wagon","microforge","Old Forge","software forge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b30cf63e3954d7a902","definition":"The act of beating or working iron or steel.","example":"In the greater bodies the forge was easy.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["American forge","brute de forge","Catalan forge","Clifton Forge","Consall Forge","forge-hammer","forgelike","forgeman","forgemaster","Forge Valley","forge wagon","microforge","Old Forge","software forge"],"source":"Englis